   = note: Text is a view wherever a view suffices, and the ledger records whether a published parameter is lent or kept and what a result points into (ADR-282 D2). Only an `extern "C"` declaration and a `pub extern fn` write `ref String`, as the pointer C expects.
   = help: Write `String` without `ref`.
error[NK1104]: You're returning `ref String`, but the function is declared to return `String`.
  --> tests/a_pub_function_refuses_the_view_arm_of_a_let.nika:8:12
   |
 8 |     return y
   |            ^
   |
   = note: This is a view: it points into text that something else owns.
   = note: The function returns it, and the caller keeps it after the call ends, so it needs text of its own.
   = note: Nikaia never copies text behind your back: a copy costs as much as the text is long, so it's written where it happens.
   = help: Write `.clone()` to copy it here.
